abstract: >
  Function Tunnel Networks (FTN) is an open research framework
  exploring how stable functional pathways shape intelligence,
  learning, specialization, education, division of labor,
  comparative advantage, collective intelligence, and Human-AI
  collaboration. Building upon Function Tunnel Intelligence (FTI),
  the framework introduces Function Tunnel Networks and Function
  Tunnel Capital as structural mechanisms for understanding the
  accumulation and evolution of capabilities across individuals,
  organizations, societies, and Human-AI systems.

